# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

A terminal UI application built from the `~/scripts/tui-cli-template/bash/` scaffold.

## Requirements

- Bash 4.2+
- A real TTY (will not work when stdin or stdout are piped)
- A terminal that supports truecolor (24-bit) ANSI — all modern terminals qualify

## Running

```bash
chmod +x main.sh      # once, after scaffolding
bash main.sh          # explicit interpreter
./main.sh             # or directly if executable
```

## Navigation keys

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `1`–`9` | Select numbered item |
| `?` | Help screen |
| `b` | Back (return to parent menu) |
| `q` | Quit (works from any menu) |
| Enter | Ignored (re-prompts) |

Arrow keys are **not** used. Navigation is purely by number/letter keys pressed once — no Enter needed.

## File structure

```
.
├── main.sh              # Entry point — sources lib/, runs main_menu
└── lib/
    ├── colors.sh        # Readonly ANSI escape constants (Nord palette)
    ├── screen.sh        # clear_screen, render_header, render_footer
    ├── menu.sh          # render_menu, read_choice, flash
    └── screens/
        ├── home.sh      # main_menu — top-level dispatch (1/2/?/q)
        └── detail.sh    # detail_menu — example nested list (1-5/b/q)
```

## Extending

1. Add `lib/screens/<name>.sh` with a `<name>_menu()` function.
2. Guard it with `[[ -n "${_NAME_SH_LOADED:-}" ]] && return 0; readonly _NAME_SH_LOADED=1`.
3. Source it in `main.sh` after the other screens.
4. Add a dispatch case in `main_menu` (in `lib/screens/home.sh`) to call it.

Use `render_header`, `render_menu`, `read_choice`, and `flash` from `lib/menu.sh` for consistent
styling. Add new constants to `lib/colors.sh` using existing Nord variables; never hard-code hex
values inline.

## Nord colour palette

| Constant | Role | Hex |
|----------|------|-----|
| `$ACCENT` | Menu keys, highlights | `#88C0D0` |
| `$OK` | Success messages | `#A3BE8C` |
| `$ERR` | Error / invalid input | `#BF616A` |
| `$MUTED` | Decorative lines | `#3B4252` |
| `$NORD4` | Body text | `#D8DEE9` |

